            "paragraph": "We distinguish two variants of the GlaUnTI model. The first one (Model C) is the model where all glacier facies predictors are replaced with a placeholder (\u22121 for each grid cell and facies channel), i.e. only the initial guess, glacier geometry and climate aggregates influence the correction terms. The second one (Model D) is where the actual values of GF are fed to the model where available, and the placeholder is used elsewhere, allowing for separate evaluation of the added value of glacier facies maps. Both variants have frozen TI parameters from trained Model A. The initial parameters of Model C are random, while those of Model D are initialised from trained Model C.",
